WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:00.030
<b>Summary of previous episodes</b>

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:06.410
<i>Last time on </i>Frankenstein Family<i>...</i>

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:11.450
<i>We started living with our landlord.</i>

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:14.700
<i>He invited us on a trip out to the mountains.</i>

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:21.520
<i>My sisters took the medicine 
that let them appear human,</i>

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:23.800
<i>and we went out to a nearby mountain.</i>

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.800
<i>I ran into Sumire-chan there, too!</i>

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:33.900
<i>It was awesome, almost 
like a real date, but...</i>

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:40.520
<i>Aisuri-neesan started acting strangely,</i>

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:44.410
<i>so Snow-niisan and I went to search for her.</i>

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:47.980
<i>I hope nothing goes wrong, but...</i>

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:23.210
<b>Frankenstein Family</b>

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:42.450
<b>#7: Sisters</b>

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:53.800
Snow!

00:02:57.570 --> 00:02:59.320
Turn human already!

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:01.650
Hide and seek again?

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:03.150
Got it!

00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:04.060
Yeah!

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:09.160
Rock-paper-scissors!

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:10.650
Yeah—

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:12.970
The odd man out is "it"!

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.520
Count all the way to 10, okay?

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:33.820
There are too many smells here...

00:03:56.970 --> 00:04:01.670
I know. Let's play hide-and-seek 
like we used to, Aisuri...

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:23.200
Found you...

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:45.110
So fast!

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:55.550
Okay. I'll help find Aisuri, too!

00:04:58.420 --> 00:05:00.690
I don't think she's over here!

00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:03.400
She might be hiding at home!

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:08.200
Wh-Why are you coming at me?!

00:05:16.570 --> 00:05:18.210
You're Aisuri, right?

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:24.090
Aw... how'd you know?

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.670
How could you tell?

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:33.000
Because you're both completely different.

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:48.390
Your hair... it's all messed up.

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:08.090
Dammit! I can't believe he 
found us out that quick!

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:10.590
Maybe they really <i>can</i> tell?

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:12.430
Next time, for sure—

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:14.280
Look out!

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:18.890
Are you okay?

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:19.910
Yeah...

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:27.350
Mama! Mama! Emergency!

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:31.290
My hair's all whirly!

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.450
Is she gonna die?!

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:35.240
Oh, you touched that fluid?

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:38.820
What's this? What have you 
been up to, all in secret?

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:41.600
Hey, is Aisuri going to die?

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:42.460
No.

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:46.540
Oh, thank goodness!

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:48.970
But what is this?!

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:51.450
A formula for changing hair type.

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:56.180
It was so powerful that the hair never 
turned back, so we halted our research.

00:06:56.180 --> 00:06:59.560
Oh, no! Mama, you gotta keep researching it!

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:01.690
Turn my hair back to normal!

00:07:04.010 --> 00:07:05.310
I can't.

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:09.740
I'm not interested in it anymore, after all.

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:13.350
If you hate it so much, why don't you 
and Ashisu both shave your heads?

00:07:13.850 --> 00:07:15.580
Slick and shiny!

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:17.350
Slick and shiny?!

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:28.590
We're not coming down from here 
until you turn my hair back!

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:30.370
She seems pretty mad.

00:07:30.370 --> 00:07:32.840
That's impressive craftsmanship, though.

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:34.180
We'll leave them be.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:37.410
A child's tantrum can't 
last more than two days.

00:07:37.410 --> 00:07:40.930
True! This is an important 
time for Suishi, too.

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:43.430
They left!

00:07:43.430 --> 00:07:47.000
Ashisu, you'll fight with me, right?

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:50.440
Yeah!

00:07:50.930 --> 00:07:52.510
Of course I will!

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:17.180
I want us to be the same.

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:27.490
<i>To talk together.</i>

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:29.270
<i>To eat together.</i>

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:31.280
<i>To play together.</i>

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:33.200
<i>To sleep together.</i>

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:35.660
<i>Because...</i>

00:08:37.860 --> 00:08:39.930
<i>since the day we were born...</i>

00:08:39.930 --> 00:08:41.450
<i>we have always been together.</i>

00:08:42.950 --> 00:08:44.890
<i>Even if our powers are different,</i>

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:48.790
<i>we know.</i>

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:51.950
<i>We are the same!</i>

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:58.430
No matter what you look 
like, you're still Aisuri.

00:09:22.550 --> 00:09:23.870
Help!

00:09:28.740 --> 00:09:31.770
There's a m-monster is in the forest!

00:09:31.770 --> 00:09:33.380
A huge spider!

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:36.090
Huge spider? As big as your face?

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:38.520
It was bigger than Ron!

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:42.310
Stop lying. No spider's that big.

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:44.190
We don't even get bears around here.

00:09:44.190 --> 00:09:46.100
You probably just saw a boar.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:48.100
It's true!

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:49.400
Hey, kids...

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:50.650
Excuse me!

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:55.320
Have you seen a young man 
with white hair and a boy?

00:09:56.090 --> 00:10:00.300
No, but if they're in there, 
they probably got eaten.

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:04.530
Wait, there was that girl 
who told us to run away...

00:10:04.530 --> 00:10:06.080
You don't think...

00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:09.080
Suishi-chan, let's find them.

00:10:10.310 --> 00:10:11.590
I'm not going.

00:10:12.690 --> 00:10:14.590
Aren't you worried about them, though?

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:21.050
Will you take me to the place 
you were talking about?

00:10:24.340 --> 00:10:26.060
<i>I wish he'd butt out...</i>

00:10:37.510 --> 00:10:38.590
There they are!

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:12.810
I never realized their complete forms 
had progressed to this degree...

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:16.820
You think their aggressive instincts 
collided, and it ended in a draw?

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:18.140
Or...

00:11:18.810 --> 00:11:22.070
I'd like to find a way to turn
 them back quickly, but...

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:25.070
No need to rush. They'll be
 back to normal soon.

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:31.080
I don't get a chance like this often, so while
 I'm here, I'd better do some research!

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:36.110
I might be able to create a medicine that 
preserves their human forms indefinitely!

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:55.310
I really am a genius!

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:56.340
We're back!

00:12:56.340 --> 00:12:57.790
Thank goodness!

00:12:58.890 --> 00:13:01.500
First, let's get your disguises ready.

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:08.260
Yeah! Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:11.830
They look so happy... are they that
 glad to be back to the way they were?

00:13:12.820 --> 00:13:18.780
Well... to them, the way they 
are now is the real them.

00:13:18.780 --> 00:13:23.980
If I couldn't become a dog, if you weren't 
a genius... you'd hate it, wouldn't you?

00:13:24.130 --> 00:13:26.550
Like something's missing...

00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:26.210
It would be like something's missing.

00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:27.980
Is that it?

00:13:36.850 --> 00:13:40.840
<i>If you become human, you'll be 
able to do all kinds of things!</i>

00:13:44.790 --> 00:13:45.980
<i>If...</i>

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:50.590
<i>it turns out I can't perfect the medicine,</i>

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:57.520
<i>where in the world will we find 
anyone that will accept my siblings?</i>

00:13:59.110 --> 00:14:00.940
You'll make a fine guinea pig.

00:14:08.330 --> 00:14:09.610
Mr. Landlord!

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:14.360
They're saying a giant spider 
monster showed up around here!

00:14:14.360 --> 00:14:16.120
Is everybody safe?

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:19.590
You saw it, right?!

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:24.090
Anyway... we found them, 
so let's get out of here quick!

00:14:31.110 --> 00:14:32.670
There we go!

00:14:38.680 --> 00:14:39.820
<i>I think, maybe...</i>

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:45.350
<i>maybe he'd accept us.</i>

00:14:50.150 --> 00:14:53.320
I wish I had the same hair as you, Ashisu.

00:14:53.320 --> 00:14:55.870
But I...

00:15:02.370 --> 00:15:03.820
Aisuri!

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:08.020
Come down! Let's have a snack.

00:15:08.020 --> 00:15:10.390
I gathered up all your favorite bugs!

00:15:10.390 --> 00:15:11.340
Snow...

00:15:11.700 --> 00:15:14.850
Now that I think about it, 
this is all your fault!

00:15:15.210 --> 00:15:16.260
Come with us!

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:24.270
He won't be able to guess this time.

00:15:24.670 --> 00:15:27.280
Try to guess which one is which!

00:15:28.810 --> 00:15:31.780
Why do you two want to be the same?

00:15:32.370 --> 00:15:34.280
Because we're twins.

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:37.040
Do twins have to be the same?

00:15:38.130 --> 00:15:39.330
Of course we do!

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:41.390
Because Ashisu and I are together!

00:15:41.390 --> 00:15:42.300
Still...

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:45.400
You're just changing the subject 
because you can't tell!

00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:46.170
I can tell!

00:15:46.580 --> 00:15:49.170
The one who's been talking 
all this time is Aisuri!

00:15:49.170 --> 00:15:51.880
Ashisu always does what Aisuri says.

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:54.080
So you're not the same at all!

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:55.110
And...

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:04.970
Snow, you idiot!

00:16:04.970 --> 00:16:06.900
Stop it, Aisuri.

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:10.390
Oh, Aisuri, you're so silly sometimes...

00:16:22.130 --> 00:16:24.600
Hmm? Did you come down?

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:27.800
You and Ashisu aren't together?

00:16:29.770 --> 00:16:32.060
It's okay not to be the same.

00:16:36.980 --> 00:16:38.930
<i>You're still the Aisuri I know.</i>

00:16:39.250 --> 00:16:42.860
<i>We'll always be together.</i>

00:18:13.940 --> 00:18:19.950
<b>Frankenstein Extras!</b>

00:18:14.810 --> 00:18:16.710
<i>Frankenstein Extras!</i>

00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:19.950
<b>Report No. 1</b>

00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:19.950
<i>Anime Japan Report.</i>

00:18:25.470 --> 00:18:27.660
<b></b>Yu Kaito: <b>Horie Kazuma 
</b>Ashisu:<b> Hayami Saori 
</b>Tanisu: <b>Sugiyama Riho
 </b>Suishi:<b> Ikuta Yoshiko
 </b>Sumire: <b>Kubo Yurika</b>

00:18:27.850 --> 00:18:30.690
<b>March 2018  Ariake, Tokyo</b>

00:18:31.230 --> 00:18:34.750
<b>This is Japan's biggest anime 
event, Anime Japan 2018!</b>

00:18:35.020 --> 00:18:40.720
<b>Held from March 22nd to March 25th 
with a total attendance of 152,331!</b>

00:18:41.030 --> 00:18:44.850
<b>Frankenstein Family</b>

00:18:41.030 --> 00:18:44.850
had a booth, too!

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:52.790
The corner for Sun Comics Project, the site that 
publishes <i>Frankenstein Family</i>, was also popular!

00:18:53.790 --> 00:18:56.110
<b>On March 24th, the voice cast 
did  a live talk show!</b>

00:18:56.340 --> 00:19:01.320
<b>Some familiar faces to <i>Frankenstein Extras</i> 
appeared for a pre-show discussion!</b>

00:19:01.630 --> 00:19:05.080
Such rare behind-the-scenes footage! 
They all look so serious!

00:19:07.720 --> 00:19:11.080
<b>Oh? Who is this?</b>

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:17.420
I play Yu Kaito, the landlord who takes in 
the siblings of the Frankenstein Family.

00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:18.550
<b>Yu Kaito   Voice: Horie Kazuma
32 years old, the landlord who takes in the five
 siblings and is a perpetual research student.</b>

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:18.550
My name is Horie Kazuma!

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:21.970
Wash up, then eat with us.

00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:24.250
There are lots of unusual 
things in the mountains,

00:19:24.250 --> 00:19:26.640
and the view from the top is fantastic!

00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:32.770
I'm their landlord, but I'm also what 
people call a born philanthropist.

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:35.960
I want to support and help them, 
like they were my real family.

00:19:35.960 --> 00:19:41.720
"Does such a kind man 
really exist?" You may ask.

00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:46.090
But he can be too kind, too considerate.

00:19:46.090 --> 00:19:48.280
He's the sort of guy who 
overthinks everything,

00:19:48.280 --> 00:19:50.890
so the family teases him a lot.

00:19:50.890 --> 00:19:54.630
When I play him, I wonder if 
he's a bit of a masochist.

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:56.600
He's a very kind, appealing character.

00:19:56.600 --> 00:20:01.390
So I hope you enjoy <i>Frankenstein 
Family</i> along with their landlord.

00:20:01.960 --> 00:20:06.300
Hello everyone! I'm Kubo 
Yurika, and I play Sumire!

00:20:02.280 --> 00:20:06.300
Sumire
Kubo Yurika

00:20:02.650 --> 00:20:06.300
<b>Kubo Yurika is in the wings backstage!</b>

00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:22.820
<b>Sumire  Voice: Kubo Yurika
10 years old, she ends up getting to know Tanisu after a chance meeting on the island.</b>

00:20:11.050 --> 00:20:12.360
Not gonna buy one?

00:20:12.360 --> 00:20:13.430
Um... Well...

00:20:13.430 --> 00:20:14.620
Er...

00:20:16.470 --> 00:20:18.380
Say, "Ah!"

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:22.820
Ah!

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:31.120
Sumire is the most ordinary 
girl in the whole story.

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:33.220
She's Tanisu's friend,

00:20:33.220 --> 00:20:36.150
but what will their relationship become?

00:20:36.150 --> 00:20:40.050
How will things develop 
as the story proceeds?

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:43.080
I hope you'll all watch 
and see how it turns out.

00:20:43.080 --> 00:20:44.510
See you soon!

00:20:45.530 --> 00:20:47.350
<b>It's time for the talk show!</b>

00:20:48.370 --> 00:20:51.980
<b>Is Sugiyama Rie-san... a little bit nervous?</b>

00:20:49.000 --> 00:20:51.980
Thank you all for coming!

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:53.670
Yes...

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:55.660
The most important thing here is that 
Sugiyama-san admitted to liking little boys!

00:20:53.670 --> 00:20:55.660
Yeah...

00:20:55.660 --> 00:20:56.560
Yes.

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:58.150
You really do like them, so...

00:20:58.150 --> 00:20:59.100
Yes!

00:20:59.100 --> 00:20:59.960
Isn't that amazing?

00:20:59.960 --> 00:21:02.280
And you play those parts, too!

00:21:02.280 --> 00:21:03.020
Yes.

00:21:03.020 --> 00:21:05.100
By the way, how old is too old?

00:21:05.100 --> 00:21:07.210
Why are you asking that?

00:21:07.210 --> 00:21:09.550
I think, until their voice changes.

00:21:09.550 --> 00:21:10.490
Until about then.

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:12.260
So you like your shotas!

00:21:12.260 --> 00:21:17.360
Also, during the recording, 
Mori-san wasn't there today.

00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:18.410
Yes, that's right.

00:21:18.410 --> 00:21:21.700
It was mainly girls, and you're all tall,

00:21:21.700 --> 00:21:23.750
and you all drink alcohol.

00:21:23.750 --> 00:21:26.740
I felt like Namikawa-san and 
I were driven into a corner.

00:21:26.740 --> 00:21:29.550
That's not true!

00:21:29.550 --> 00:21:31.390
The girls are all very ladylike.

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:33.050
Yes, we're very quiet.

00:21:33.050 --> 00:21:35.350
But you all change when you're drinking!

00:21:35.350 --> 00:21:36.280
Do we?

00:21:36.280 --> 00:21:37.350
Do we?

00:21:37.350 --> 00:21:39.760
Stop playing innocent!

00:21:39.760 --> 00:21:43.240
But when we drink very heavily,

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:45.610
we start talking.

00:21:45.610 --> 00:21:47.450
We tell stories, too.

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:49.210
We all talk about our performance, too.

00:21:49.210 --> 00:21:50.190
Yes, that's right.

00:21:50.190 --> 00:21:51.000
We do that a lot.

00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:53.240
I thought it was amazing.

00:21:53.240 --> 00:21:55.470
But during recording, you're 
always debating, right?

00:21:55.470 --> 00:21:56.710
Yes, we are.

00:21:56.710 --> 00:21:59.230
"This scene should go more like this."

00:21:59.230 --> 00:22:01.380
Lots of arguing among the cast.

00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:03.420
But it's not like you're fighting about it.

00:22:03.420 --> 00:22:04.210
Yes, yes.

00:22:04.210 --> 00:22:05.940
It's more like, "It should be like this."

00:22:05.940 --> 00:22:08.490
You talk with the directors.

00:22:09.990 --> 00:22:19.600
<b>In the green room after the talk show ended...</b>

00:22:13.810 --> 00:22:14.560
How is it?

00:22:14.560 --> 00:22:15.530
It's great.

00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:19.600
That's great.

00:22:19.610 --> 00:22:21.500
I was so nervous.

00:22:21.500 --> 00:22:26.760
She won't shut up about how nervous she is.

00:22:24.300 --> 00:22:26.760
Yeah, I was really annoying.

00:22:26.760 --> 00:22:30.070
I wasn't able to attend 
the meeting beforehand,

00:22:30.070 --> 00:22:32.810
but things still got really lively,

00:22:32.810 --> 00:22:35.260
so I'm grateful to have 
such reliable comrades.

00:22:35.260 --> 00:22:36.630
It was really fun.

00:22:38.580 --> 00:22:41.460
Lots of unique characters will be appearing!

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:44.590
They might all seem very silly, 
but the story is very serious.

00:22:44.590 --> 00:22:46.420
It will make you think about a lot of things.

00:22:46.420 --> 00:22:49.550
I want to be a more generous 
person, like the landlord.

00:22:49.550 --> 00:22:52.850
It's a cozy family story, 
so I hope you all watch it!

00:22:52.850 --> 00:22:56.710
We hope you keep watching 
<i>Frankenstein Family</i>!

00:22:55.390 --> 00:22:56.710
<b>Supporting</b>

00:22:55.390 --> 00:22:56.710
<b>Supporting</b>

00:22:55.390 --> 00:22:56.710
<b>Supporting</b>

00:22:56.710 --> 00:22:58.070
Did I get it wrong?!

00:22:58.070 --> 00:23:00.510
I got it wrong! I got it wrong!

00:23:00.510 --> 00:23:01.310
Take two!

00:23:01.560 --> 00:23:07.630
We hope you keep supporting 
<i>Frankenstein Family</i>!

00:23:09.900 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:10.520 --> 00:23:12.570
<i>I think the landlord is a good person.</i>

00:23:12.570 --> 00:23:15.940
<i>But even so, 
after the thing with my tutor,</i>

00:23:15.940 --> 00:23:19.970
<i>I need to be careful in determining 
whether we can really trust him.</i>

00:23:19.970 --> 00:23:24.070
<i>Then the landlord takes 
us out to buy furniture.</i>

00:23:24.070 --> 00:23:28.210
<i>He shows us all around the island... 
he's definitely a fun person!</i>

00:23:28.520 --> 00:23:32.180
<i>Oh, no! I just said I need to be
 careful in my judgment of him!</i>

00:23:32.180 --> 00:23:34.430
<i>I won't let adults fool me again!</i>

00:23:34.660 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>#8:  Observation</b>

00:23:34.920 --> 00:23:38.120
<i>Next time on </i>Frankenstein 
Family<i>: "Observation."</i>

00:23:38.120 --> 00:23:39.850
<i>Catch it, okay?</i>
